# The Docker build context is an ALLOWLIST: everything is excluded, then only what the image
# needs is let back in. A denylist would send any new secret file (an API key in the repo root,
# say) into an image layer, where it stays; tests/test_docker_context.py checks that every
# pattern in the "Secrets" section of .gitignore stays out.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!README.md
!src/
!tests/
!scripts/
!docs/

# Read by tests/test_docker_context.py, which checks this very file inside the container too.
!.gitignore
!.dockerignore
!Dockerfile

# Allowed directories can still hold things that must not ship (the host's caches, a key file
# somebody dropped into src/).
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.anthropic-key
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/.env*
